{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#",
  "$id": "https://genomicschain.ch/schemas/prov_reachability_v0_1.schema.json",
  "title": "GenomicsChain reachability observation over a Tier-2.5 provenance record, record_version 0.1",
  "description": "Synoptis evidence manifest for an observation the anchor made (design docs/design/prov_anchoring_design_v0_1.md §6.3, v0.1.15): whether the places a provenance bundle names for its environment still answer, asked from the anchor on observed_at. Counts per category (items and distinct locators, then one count per result bucket, digest_match and exists split by the class of the host the bundle wrote) and dates only. Nothing was fetched: digest_match and exists are the answer of the place itself. Locators, addresses, answers, host names and the proof_id of the prov record are not recorded; prov_proof_ref is the SHA-256 of that proof_id. A dated observation, not a grade: it says nothing about other networks, later dates, or whether the environment can be built (not_checked).",
